# 2026-11-21

- Behavior change (CloudMesh.Uuid): `Uuid.Create()` is now strictly increasing within a process, across threads.
  It implements RFC 9562 §6.2 method 1: a 16-bit counter sits directly below the 48-bit timestamp and is seeded
  randomly each millisecond, so collision resistance across processes stays about the same. Ids never go
  backwards, even if the system clock does; under extreme load they may run slightly ahead of the clock.
  The signature is unchanged.
  - Cost: about 3 ns more per id on one thread. All callers share one lock-free counter, so under heavy
    multi-threaded load throughput plateaus at roughly 35-50M ids/s per process instead of scaling with cores.
  - `Uuid.Next(...)` overloads are unchanged: they stamp the given time with random bits and don't use the counter.

# v2.0.1

- Feature: Added timeout handling to DataBlock. See the examples/DataBlocks/TimeoutSample for more information.
- Deprecation: Dropped support for dotnet 6.0 and 7.0. 
- Deprecation: Dropped support for ISystemClock and its implementations in favor of native BCL TimeProvider. They had been marked as obsolete since the release of dotnet 8.0.
- Dependency: Updated dependencies to more recent versions due to security vulnerabilities:
  - System.Text.Json: At least 9.0.0
  - System.Net.Http: At least 4.3.4
  - System.Text.RegularExpressions: At least 4.3.1